    LLM: 'Game: Aces and Kings. Logic: Complete all eight foundations, four building up from ace to king and four building down from king to ace, without regard to suit.',
    Player: 'Aces and Kings is a difficult two-deck solitaire in which eight foundations build both upward from aces and downward from kings without regard to suit.',
    objective: 'Build the foundations after dealing cards onto king-led columns, with queens excluded from play.',
    gameplay: 'Remove queens, then deal cards into columns headed by kings. As kings appear they start new columns. Available cards are moved to foundations according to the solitaire rules until the layout is solved or blocked.',
